ist":-0.06281961790478069,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.12744623622498752,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.0322499700716079,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":41.1,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06557282372593579,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":84.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.01596003992008921,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":70.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.012850151873101586,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":78.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.04619,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":30.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Southside Bancshares, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Southside Bank that provides various financial services to individuals, businesses, municipal entities, and nonprofit organizations. Its deposit products include savings, money market, and interest and noninterest bearing checking accounts, as well as certificates of deposit. The company offers consumer loan services, including 1-4 family residential, home equity, home improvement, automobile, and other consumer related loans; commercial loans, such as short-term working capital loans for inventory and accounts receivable, short and medium-term loans for equipment or other business capital expansion, commercial real estate loans, and municipal loans; and construction loans for 1-4 family residential and commercial real estate. It also provides trust and wealth management services comprising investment management, administration of irrevocable, revocable, and testamentary trusts, estate administration, and custodian services for individuals, partnerships, and corporations; brokerage services; and safe deposit services. In addition, the company offers retirement and employee benefit accounts consisting of plans and profit sharing plans; and telephone, internet, and mobile banking products. The company offers various banking services through branches, drive-thru facilities, loan production offices, automated teller machines, and interactive teller machines. Southside Bancshares, Inc. was founded in 1960 and is headquartered in Tyler, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Keith M. Donahoe | CEO, President & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $972,282 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 781 people. Revenue per employee of $304K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $94K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Southside Bancshares, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.0B market cap on $237M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 9% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $73M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 31 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.36\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 50% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","27 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Southside Bancshares (NYSE:SBSI) CAO April Pinkley Sells 6,724 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/southside-bancshares-nysesbsi-cao-april-pinkley-sells-6724-shares-of-stock.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793988539.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.883,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Southside Bancshares declares $0.37 dividend (NYSE:SBSI)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4667717-southside-bancshares-declares-0_37-dividend","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793935832.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Southside Bancshares (SBSI) Climbed, So What Is Behind The Move?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/southside-bancshares-sbsi-climbed-behind-221025446.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793916625.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.856,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Earnings Estimates Moving Higher for Southside Bancshares (SBSI): Time to Buy?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3020918/earnings-estimates-moving-higher-for-southside-bancshares-sbsi-time-to-buy?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_8-3020918","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793636402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","m_and_a"]},{"title":"Southside Bancshares (SBSI) Upgraded to Strong Buy: Here's What You Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3020874/southside-bancshares-sbsi-upgraded-to-s